      "description": "A Bristol native, graffiti artist Banksy has acquired worldwide fame for his thought-provoking and satirical street art, with several original pieces still remaining across the city.\n\nThe Bristol Tour Map of Banksy is an interactive guide to the remaining Banksy artwork in Bristol; pinpointing your location and providing directions to every artwork site. With background information, photos, location markers, and Google Maps navigation built in, this is the essential guide for discovering Banksy artwork across Bristol.\n\nFeaturing all the most well-known and central artwork pieces, spanning the City Centre, Harbourside, Park Street and beyond, this app is the perfect companion for an immersive walk around Bristol.\n\nDesigned specifically for use on the move, the app makes it easy to see your location in relation to nearby artwork sites, and even launch navigation directions directly from within the app.\n\nKey app features include:\n\nALL BANKSY’S IN BRISTOL 2026\n\n• All locations fully checked and updated for 2026\n• Newly reviewed artwork information and updated site details across the app\n\nMULTILINGUAL SUPPORT\n\n• English\n• Spanish\n• French\n• Polish\n• Chinese\n• German\n• Dutch\n\nINTERACTIVE MAP\n\n• Interactive geolocation map pinpointing all Banksy artwork and distance from your location\n• View the next nearest artwork location in real time as you move\n• Navigate by the nearest artwork to you with live distance updates\n• Complete navigation directions (walking, public transport, and driving) to all locations\n• Easily explore and discover artwork while on the move\n\nARTWORK HISTORY\n\n• Background history and photos for all Bristol artworks\n• Further reading links to related articles and points of interest\n• Sight-spotting tips to help you locate artwork when visiting sites\n\nOFFLINE APP\n\n• No internet connection required to view saved location information and photos\n\nFAVOURITES\n\n• Save your favourite artwork locations for quick future access",
